This is a minimal base62 demo chart (discussion #860).

Lines that do not begin with "#" are ignored by the BMS parser, so this
paragraph is just documentation.

Because of "#BASE 62", keysound IDs are CASE-SENSITIVE: "Aa", "AA", and "aA"
are three different sounds. On a base-36 chart they would all collapse to the
same sound. Drop this folder into the Bemuse custom-chart / preview area
(alongside the referenced .wav/.ogg files) to hear three distinct keysounds.

#PLAYER 1
#GENRE Demo
#TITLE base62 keysound demo
#ARTIST bemuse
#BASE 62
#BPM 120
#PLAYLEVEL 1
#RANK 3

#WAVAa kick.wav
#WAVAA snare.wav
#WAVaA hat.wav

#00111:AaAAaA00
